wavy|curved-pattern|ADJECTIVE|having a series of curves|Having repeated gentle curves rather than being straight.|gợn sóng; lượn sóng|She drew a wavy line below the heading.|Cô ấy vẽ một đường lượn sóng dưới tiêu đề.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; wavy hair describes curved shape, not wetness.|-
decent|adequate|ADJECTIVE|good enough for a purpose|Of a reasonably good standard or sufficient for a need.|khá tốt; đủ dùng|We found a decent room within our budget.|Chúng tôi tìm được một phòng khá tốt trong khả năng chi trả.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; decent need not mean excellent.|0
decent|respectable|ADJECTIVE|behaving fairly and respectfully|Behaving in a fair, respectful, or morally acceptable way.|đàng hoàng; tử tế|It was decent of him to return the lost wallet.|Anh ấy thật tử tế khi trả lại chiếc ví bị mất.|Decent of someone to do something evaluates an action; distinct from adequate quality.|1
elastic|stretch-and-return|ADJECTIVE|able to stretch and return towards its shape|Able to stretch under force and return towards the previous shape when the force is removed.|đàn hồi; co giãn|The elastic cuff stretched easily over her hand.|Cổ tay áo co giãn dễ dàng giãn ra để bàn tay cô ấy luồn qua.|Before a material or object noun; elastic here is an adjective, not the related material noun.|-
moving|emotional-effect|ADJECTIVE|causing strong feelings|Causing strong feelings, especially sympathy or sadness.|cảm động; gây xúc động|Her account of the reunion was deeply moving.|Lời kể của cô ấy về cuộc đoàn tụ rất cảm động.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; moving describes the cause, while moved can describe the affected person.|0
moving|in-motion|ADJECTIVE|changing position|Changing position rather than remaining still.|đang chuyển động; đang di chuyển|The photographer waited for the moving boat to pass.|Nhiếp ảnh gia chờ chiếc thuyền đang di chuyển đi qua.|Participial adjective before a noun in this sense; not the emotional meaning.|1
postpone|delay-plan|VERB|move a planned event to a later time|To arrange for something planned to happen later than originally intended.|hoãn; dời lại|They postponed the outdoor concert until the following weekend.|Họ hoãn buổi hòa nhạc ngoài trời đến cuối tuần sau.|Transitive postpone an event; postpone doing something uses an ing form, and until introduces the later time.|0
